    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The arts, specifically music education, struggles to survive within the curriculum of many public schools. Despite its statistically supported benefits as well as positive testimonials by students who participated in such programs, under an economic recession and the STEM-focused curriculum set by many states under the common-core standards, programs continue to be decimated. This research-based argument calls to action longitudinal studies by universities to determine a method in which to measure the effectivity of a music program to affirm its credibility in the curriculum, as well as stress both the intellectual and creative benefits that derive from such an education.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
